{
  "requirement": "Overrides the SDK’s OpenAI model, endpoint, credentials, or inference options. Omitted settings use the defaults in the agent configuration contract.\n\n```rust,ignore\n#[non_exhaustive]\npub struct OpenAiConfig {\n    pub model: Option<String>,\n    pub endpoint: Option<String>,\n    pub api_key_env: Option<String>,\n    pub api_key: Option<SecretString>,\n    pub options: BTreeMap<String, OptionValue>,\n}\n\nimpl OpenAiConfig {\n    pub fn new() -> Self;\n    pub fn model(self, model: String) -> Self;\n    pub fn endpoint(self, endpoint: String) -> Self;\n    pub fn api_key_env(self, api_key_env: String) -> Self;\n    pub fn api_key(self, api_key: SecretString) -> Self;\n    pub fn option(self, key: String, value: OptionValue) -> Self;\n}\n```\n\nTrait implementations\n\n```rust,ignore\nimpl Clone for OpenAiConfig;\nimpl Debug for OpenAiConfig;\nimpl Default for OpenAiConfig;\nimpl<'de> Deserialize<'de> for OpenAiConfig;\nimpl PartialEq for OpenAiConfig;\nimpl Serialize for OpenAiConfig;\n```",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "I found no test-adequacy gap for `requirements.sdk.graph.agent-harness.OpenAiConfig`. I read the supplied tests and the implementation excerpts for the struct and its impls in `crates/trust-but-verify/src/agent/config.rs`. I also read `requirements.sdk.graph.agent-harness.agent_config.settings`, which defines the defaults.\n\nObligations and the tests that cover them:\n\n- **Struct fields and builders.** `new()` starts empty, and each builder sets only its own field. Calling `option` again with the same key replaces the value and keeps the others. `mod[tests]/fn[backend_builders_set_only_the_requested_fields]` asserts that `OpenAiConfig::new()` serializes to `{}`. It then sets model, endpoint, `api_key_env`, `api_key` and options, and asserts the exact JSON, including `a` replaced by 2 and `b` kept.\n- **Omitted settings use the defaults.**\n  - Model and endpoint: `mod[tests]/fn[option_defaults_and_credential_resolution_are_deterministic]` asserts `gpt-6.1-sol` and `https://api.openai.com/v1`.\n  - Default credential variable: `mod[tests]/fn[openai_uses_the_default_credential_variable]` re-runs itself in a child process with `OPENAI_API_KEY` set. It asserts that `OpenAiConfig::new().resolved_api_key()` returns that value. It sets the environment only in the child, so it does not touch process-wide state.\n  - Default options: `mod[tests]/fn[openai_inference_options_only_fill_missing_defaults]` covers `max_output_tokens` 16384 and `reasoning.effort` low. It also checks that user-supplied options are not overridden and that a partial `reasoning` map is filled in.\n- **Overrides.**\n  - Credentials: the same `option_defaults_and_credential_resolution_are_deterministic` test checks that a custom `api_key_env` that is absent produces an error naming it. It also checks that an explicit `api_key` is used.\n  - Model, endpoint and options reach the backend: `supplied_openai_backend_runs_independent_calls_against_a_local_transport` in `crates/trust-but-verify/src/agent/configured.rs` asserts the request model `local-test`, and the call goes to a local endpoint. It also asserts `max_output_tokens` 16384 in the requests, and that the API key does not leak into saved evidence.\n- **Trait implementations.**\n  - `Serialize`, `Deserialize` and `PartialEq`: `mod[tests]/fn[all_backends_preserve_nested_settings_and_credentials]` round-trips an OpenAI config with model, endpoint, `api_key` and nested options. It asserts equality of the JSON and of the deserialized copy. `mod[tests]/fn[openai_inference_options_only_fill_missing_defaults]` also deserializes a minimal config and compares it with `OpenAiConfig::new()`.\n  - `Default`: used by `new()` and asserted through `OpenAiConfig::default()` in `option_defaults_and_credential_resolution_are_deterministic`.\n  - `Clone` and `Debug`: both are plain `#[derive]`s with no conditional and no transformation of their own. The `<redacted>` behavior belongs to `SecretString`, which a different requirement governs.\n- **Public surface.** `crates/trust-but-verify/tests/public_api.rs#fn[public_exports_match_the_appendix]` checks that the exported type matches the specification.\n\nI found no requirement-violating behavior that these assertions would accept.",
